\n- Then set back to \"aaa\". See if errors clear.\n\nThis checks the \"compared on every keystroke in either one\" thoroughly. If errors are stale in more ways, report maybe as part of same bug (already logged, but a separate observation might be duplicate). Let's do it for thoroughness; if another distinct bug appears (e.g., OK stays enabled when mismatched), that's important since it could allow encryption with wrong passphrase.\n\nImportant: if OK remains enabled after making them mismatch (when previously matched), that's a serious bug — user could encrypt with mismatched passphrase. Let's test.\n\nClose FAB menu first (BACK). Then open Encrypt on QA_Orig.txt via 3-dot... but 3-dot unreachable. Use long-press → More options doesn't have Encrypt. Hmm. I need the quick context menu via 3-dot for Encrypt. For QA_Orig at y=2095, unreachable. Alternative: scroll list so QA_Orig's 3-dot is at a reachable y. Scroll up (finger down) to bring rows down? The list is at top already. The row list is long. If I scroll down (finger up), QA_Orig moves up to reachable positions. Let's swipe up a bit then tap its 3-dot.\n\nPress BACK to close FAB, then swipe up ~0.2 to move QA_Orig up. Then tap its 3-dot."}
